<title>INDIA: India approves ILFS proposal to set up fund.</title>
<headline>India approves ILFS proposal to set up fund.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's Industry Ministry said on Monday it approved a proposal by Infrastructure Leasing and Financial Services Ltd (ILFS) to set up a direct investment fund.</p>
<p>The investment fund will have a foreign direct investment of 3.5 billion rupees, a ministry statement said.</p>
<p>The statement did not give other details.</p>
<p>($1=35.70 rupees)</p>
